📋 1. Architecture OverviewThe Typing feature utilizes an Enterprise Metadata-Driven Pattern. State management is split cleanly into two structural slices:typingSlice: Manages entity records data streams, infinite scroll pagination state, and active view filter routes (course vs test).typingFormSlice: A reusable utility slice that tracks active UI popups (manage and delete) using standard string index properties (domain) to switch context automatically.🧩 2. Component Specifications🟦 Component A: TypingPageThe main orchestrator component responsible for syncing lookups, resetting state on contextual pivots, and presenting the context control headers.Main Functions & HooksContext Setup: Evaluates domain = FORM_DOMAINS.TYPINGS to configure state targeting down the tree.Static Sync: Synchronizes initial metadata options (fetchLessons and fetchDurations) globally exactly once when mounted.Route Pivot Sync: Detects changes in the Next.js route property, invalidating stale arrays via resetTypingState, flipping target modes via setFilterMode, and triggering an initial page fetch.Popup Dispatcher: Passes dynamic fallback fields (defaults) to pre-select a default typing session duration if the active route is a course exercise.🟩 Component B: RenderTypingA heavy list presentation layer optimized for large record streams. It handles inline action event routing and hosts infinite list scroll intersection nodes.Main Functions & HooksDynamic Data Query: Resolves structural lists (selectFilteredTypings) and active chunk meta fields from the store.useInfiniteScroll: Monitors intersection visibility fields against global loader criteria (isInitialLoading || isFetchingMore) and page termination limits (pagination?.hasMore). Increments next page requests automatically.Action Routing: Dispatches openManagePopup containing active rows inside an editData property block to bypass entity instantiation pipelines completely when executing modifications.🟨 Component C: ManageTypingPopupA unified data capture modal operating on shared form objects. It supports layout swapping, programmatic lock downs, and input calculations.Main Functions & HooksDynamic Title/Data Mapping: Resolves lessons, dynamic validation logic, and text titles instantly from a specialized selectTypingResultMeta selector.Form Control: Forwards form target values straight into a slice key map through single updateFormField structural dispatches.Property Constraints & Interventions:Locks drop-down controls (disabled={route === "course"}) if editing or adding standard typing practices.Prevents submission requests via explicit validation boundaries if an application user sets a net speed integer higher than a gross speed integer.Formats text payloads and sanitizes types using native JS conversion utilities (Number(), parseFloat()) prior to launching async thunk dispatches.🟥 Component D: DeleteTypingPopupA smart state wrapper container encapsulating destructive entity deletion streams. It handles background state tracking and connects straight to standard presentational elements.Main Functions & HooksContext Isolation: Uses selectDeletePopupMeta(state, domain) to track whether it is open without mixing up context with other delete modals in the app.Safe Destruction: Extracts deep reference variables through short-circuit chains (item?.exercise?.title) to shield presentation containers from UI lifecycle initialization runtime crashes.⚙️ 3. Functionality & Lifecycle MatricesState Mapping MatrixThe active functional data dependencies utilize specific keys across layers:Target ContextTarget Domain String ValueTarget Redux Store PathActive UI Action HandlersTyping ResultsFORM_DOMAINS.TYPINGS ("typings")state.typingForm.typingscreateTyping / updateTyping / deleteTypingField Schema Validation SpecificationsSanitation rules enforce specific boundaries inside ManageTypingPopup:gross: Coerced via Number(val) || 0net: Coerced via Number(val) || 0 (Cannot exceed gross)accuracy: Coerced via parseFloat(val) || 0📊 4. Core Component FlowchartThis architecture design chart maps component initialization pathways, state lookup triggers, and async operational cycles inside the module.

